      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Three cases of acetabular dysplasia associated with failed ossification of the ischiopubic synchondrosis are presented. The patients are second-degree relatives and all skeletally mature with no evidence of other pathological process to delay ossification. A summary of the development of the inferior pubic ramus is presented and the literature of this unusual condition is reviewed."},
